[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2936796541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095#issuecomment-2936796541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107095","id":2936796541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vC_V9","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T19:11:46Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T19:21:51Z","body":"Probably due to floating point precision limitations, but in this case almost certainly due to:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98750\n\nCC @aaronfranke \n\nThis is a bit of a regression in usability, even though the results are *technically* more \"correct\", as `1.2` is not representable as a floating point value, it's `1.001100110011...`, so `1.2000000000000002` and `1.1999999999970896` are the immediate neighbors of this value, off by one bit (`0.02` is also not repsesentable in binary)\n\nThis *might* be an instability issue with the algorithm though","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2936796541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2936957987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095#issuecomment-2936957987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107095","id":2936957987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vDmwj","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T19:55:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T19:55:34Z","body":"This is actually a bug in Godot's editor sliders, not a bug in the String serialization algorithm. Proof: Add this to your script:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(String.num_scientific(1.2)) # Prints \"1.2\"\n\tprint(String.num_scientific(number_a)) # Prints \"1.2000000000000002\"\n\tprint(String.num_scientific(number_b)) # Prints \"1.1999999999970896\"\n\tprint(number_a == 1.2) # Prints \"false\"\n\tprint(number_b == 1.2) # Prints \"false\"\n```\n\nThe bug in Godot's editor sliders was masked before by the lack of precision in the String serialization, but it was still there.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2936957987/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2971606565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095#issuecomment-2971606565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107095","id":2971606565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xHx4l","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T20:32:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T20:32:26Z","body":"That's indeed problem with sliders, or or maybe with Range.\n\nHere's a print of \"real\" value (using `%0.20f`) and serialized value, from slider:\n`1.20000000000000017764` `1.2000000000000002`\nSame, but the value is set 